[00:04.00]What we can see in the picture is a young woman,
[00:09.00]who stands for the online dealers,
[00:11.40]is blowing a balloon with the word
[00:14.34]“commitment” on it. While a consumer shrinks
[00:18.65]at the sight of this giant balloon,
[00:20.61]fearing that it might burst.
[00:22.30]Obviously, this picture aims to criticize
[00:25.88]those dishonest online businesses
[00:29.23]which induce people to buy with empty promises.
[00:33.19]Shopping on the Internet has become an ingredient
[00:37.12]of our life thanks to the prevalence of the cyberspace.
[00:40.30]The superiority of online shopping is evident.
[00:44.19]People can compare prices without bothering
[00:47.09]to walking from one shop to another
[00:49.44]and make decisions independent of salespeople's
[00:53.08]endless persuasion. They can just settle themselves
[00:56.71]in a comfortable chair, have a cup of tea,
[00:59.05]click the mouse, and then everything is arranged.
[01:02.43]Nevertheless, sometimes shoppers find the products
[01:06.17]they receive are different from
[01:07.92]those shown on the computer screen;
[01:09.58]what's more, if goods they buy from
